  23:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/BSP/STM32N6570-DK/stm32n6570_discovery_xspi.c ****    (#) This driver is used to drive the MX66UW1G45G Octal NOR and the APS256XX Octal PSRAM
  24:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/BSP/STM32N6570-DK/stm32n6570_discovery_xspi.c ****        external memories mounted on STM32N6570-DK board.
  25:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/BSP/STM32N6570-DK/stm32n6570_discovery_xspi.c **** 
  26:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/BSP/STM32N6570-DK/stm32n6570_discovery_xspi.c ****    (#) This driver need specific component driver (MX66UW1G45G and APS256XX) to be included with.
  27:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/BSP/STM32N6570-DK/stm32n6570_discovery_xspi.c **** 
  28:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/BSP/STM32N6570-DK/stm32n6570_discovery_xspi.c ****    (#) MX66UW1G45G Initialization steps:
  29:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/BSP/STM32N6570-DK/stm32n6570_discovery_xspi.c ****        (++) Initialize the XSPI external memory using the BSP_XSPI_NOR_Init() function. This
  30:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/BSP/STM32N6570-DK/stm32n6570_discovery_xspi.c ****             function includes the MSP layer hardware resources initialization and the
  31:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/BSP/STM32N6570-DK/stm32n6570_discovery_xspi.c ****             XSPI interface with the external memory.
  32:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/BSP/STM32N6570-DK/stm32n6570_discovery_xspi.c **** 
  33:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/BSP/STM32N6570-DK/stm32n6570_discovery_xspi.c ****    (#) MX66UW1G45G Octal NOR memory operations
  34:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/BSP/STM32N6570-DK/stm32n6570_discovery_xspi.c ****        (++) XSPI memory can be accessed with read/write operations once it is
  35:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/BSP/STM32N6570-DK/stm32n6570_discovery_xspi.c ****             initialized.
  36:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/BSP/STM32N6570-DK/stm32n6570_discovery_xspi.c ****             Read/write operation can be performed with AHB access using the functions
  37:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/BSP/STM32N6570-DK/stm32n6570_discovery_xspi.c ****             BSP_XSPI_NOR_Read()/BSP_XSPI_NOR_Write().
  38:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/BSP/STM32N6570-DK/stm32n6570_discovery_xspi.c ****        (++) The function BSP_XSPI_NOR_GetInfo() returns the configuration of the XSPI memory.
  39:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/BSP/STM32N6570-DK/stm32n6570_discovery_xspi.c ****             (see the XSPI memory data sheet)
  40:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/BSP/STM32N6570-DK/stm32n6570_discovery_xspi.c ****        (++) Perform erase block operation using the function BSP_XSPI_NOR_Erase_Block() and by
  41:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/BSP/STM32N6570-DK/stm32n6570_discovery_xspi.c ****             specifying the block address. You can perform an erase operation of the whole
  42:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/BSP/STM32N6570-DK/stm32n6570_discovery_xspi.c ****             chip by calling the function BSP_XSPI_NOR_Erase_Chip().
  43:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/BSP/STM32N6570-DK/stm32n6570_discovery_xspi.c ****        (++) The function BSP_XSPI_NOR_GetStatus() returns the current status of the XSPI memory.
  44:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/BSP/STM32N6570-DK/stm32n6570_discovery_xspi.c ****             (see the XSPI memory data sheet)
  45:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/BSP/STM32N6570-DK/stm32n6570_discovery_xspi.c ****        (++) The memory access can be configured in memory-mapped mode with the call of
  46:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/BSP/STM32N6570-DK/stm32n6570_discovery_xspi.c ****             function BSP_XSPI_NOR_EnableMemoryMapped(). To go back in indirect mode, the
  47:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/BSP/STM32N6570-DK/stm32n6570_discovery_xspi.c ****             function BSP_XSPI_NOR_DisableMemoryMapped() should be used.
  48:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/BSP/STM32N6570-DK/stm32n6570_discovery_xspi.c ****        (++) The erase operation can be suspend and resume with using functions
  49:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/BSP/STM32N6570-DK/stm32n6570_discovery_xspi.c ****             BSP_XSPI_NOR_SuspendErase() and BSP_XSPI_NOR_ResumeErase()
  50:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/BSP/STM32N6570-DK/stm32n6570_discovery_xspi.c ****        (++) It is possible to put the memory in deep power-down mode to reduce its consumption.
  51:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/BSP/STM32N6570-DK/stm32n6570_discovery_xspi.c ****             For this, the function BSP_XSPI_NOR_EnterDeepPowerDown() should be called. To leave
  52:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/BSP/STM32N6570-DK/stm32n6570_discovery_xspi.c ****             the deep power-down mode, the function BSP_XSPI_NOR_LeaveDeepPowerDown() should be call
  53:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/BSP/STM32N6570-DK/stm32n6570_discovery_xspi.c ****        (++) The function BSP_XSPI_NOR_ReadID() returns the identifier of the memory
